### Variables
# Adjust @paymentsUrl to wherever your paymentRouter is mounted (e.g. /api/payments)
@baseUrl = http://localhost:5000/api
@paymentsUrl = {{baseUrl}}/payments
@phoneNumber = 0710000000
@bookingId = 115
@email = test@example.com

### 1. Direct M-Pesa prompt (replaces STK Push)
# Sends the "Enter PIN" prompt to the phone. Amount comes from the booking in the DB.
# Needs PAYSTACK_SECRET_KEY in .env and M-Pesa enabled on your Paystack account.
# Copy the "reference" from the response into @reference below.
###
POST {{paymentsUrl}}/paystack/mpesa
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "phoneNumber": "{{phoneNumber}}",
  "bookingId": {{bookingId}},
  "email": "{{email}}"
}


### 2. Hosted checkout (M-Pesa + card)
# Returns "authorizationUrl". Open it in the browser to pay.
POST {{paymentsUrl}}/paystack/initialize
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "bookingId": {{bookingId}},
  "email": "{{email}}"
}


### 3. Verify a payment (use the reference from step 1 or 2)
# This is the backup if the webhook is late. It records success or failure.
@reference = TS-115-1791997364980
GET {{paymentsUrl}}/paystack/verify/{{reference}}


### 4. Check booking status (your existing endpoint, unchanged)
GET {{paymentsUrl}}/booking-status/{{bookingId}}


### 5. Webhook test
# The webhook needs a valid x-paystack-signature (HMAC SHA512 of the raw body),
# which a .http file can't compute. Use the script instead:
#   node paystack-webhook-test.js <reference>
# Use a REAL test-mode reference from step 1 or 2: the server re-verifies
# with Paystack, so a made-up reference will be ignored.
#
# Unsigned request, should be rejected with 401:
### 5. Webhook test (Unsigned request, should be rejected with 401)
# POST http://localhost:5000/api/payments/paystack/webhook
# Content-Type: application/json
# x-paystack-signature: a6bc5ebc15f7f50c4c758d4528dd50bfcc61e7aed8a65296d6932c2c8672d79e93f4cffdf7e2bcd2e03191cf2a060cbcc512ccf237f86baf7ef042c702a0782e

# { 
#   "event": "charge.success", 
#   "data": { "reference": "{{reference}}" } 
# }

POST http://localhost:5000/api/payments/paystack/webhook
Content-Type: application/json
x-paystack-signature: a6bc5ebc15f7f50c4c758d4528dd50bfcc61e7aed8a65296d6932c2c8672d79e93f4cffdf7e2bcd2e03191cf2a060cbcc512ccf237f86baf7ef042c702a0782e

{
  "event": "charge.success",
  "data": {
    "reference": "TS-115-1791997364980"
  }
}


### Variables
@baseUrl = http://localhost:5000/api/payments
@ngrokUrl = https://unsunburned-succulently-markita.ngrok-free.dev/api/payments
@bookingId = 122
# Copy the reference from the bookings table (checkout_request_id), e.g. TS-122-1792009610531
@reference = TS-122-1792009610531


### STEP 5: is the webhook route reachable through ngrok?
# Expected: 401 {"error":"Missing signature"}
# 404 = wrong URL path, 400 = body parsing problem
POST {{ngrokUrl}}/paystack/webhook
Content-Type: application/json

{}


### STEP 7a: ask Paystack for the real payment status (this also records the payment)
# Expected when paid: {"reference":"TS-...","status":"success"}
GET {{baseUrl}}/paystack/verify/{{reference}}


### STEP 7b: what the frontend polls (should show "Confirmed" after success)
GET {{baseUrl}}/booking-status/{{bookingId}}


### Local test (expected: 401 {"error":"Missing signature"})
POST http://localhost:5000/api/payments/paystack/webhook
Content-Type: application/json

{}